# Audit debt — add every fuckup to handoff

When **Audit** fails coordinator trust (half-ass pass, wrong log file, missed static bug, thin handoff, false blame, skipped SKILL/Grok, PASS without line proof), **record it** and **paste the running list** into **every** BUILDER HANDOFF until the audit failure class is closed.

## Record format (one line each)

```
AUDIT-FAIL | YYYY-MM-DD | what audit did wrong | what it caused | fix for next audit | status: OPEN|CLOSED
```

## Where to keep the list

- Project file: `QuestTracker-Modded/AUDIT_DEBT.md` — append on every audit fuckup; mark CLOSED when next audit proves the class is fixed.
- Every **BUILDER HANDOFF** must include:

```
AUDIT DEBT (audit must not repeat):
  <paste all OPEN rows>
  <last 3 CLOSED rows for context>
```

## When to append (auditor duty)

- Coordinator says audit lied / half-assed / skipped corners
- Builder **AUDIT REJECTED** handoff (gate in builder-audit-handoff-gate.mdc)
- PASS issued but log/screenshot contradicts PASS
- Claimed `quest_tracker_log.txt` proof but only `re2_framework_log.txt` had data (or log wiped/truncated — say which file was actually read)
- Static bug obvious in grep (forward-ref, wiring) but audit did not flag before ship
- Symptom-only handoff with no file:line or L## refs

## Auditor handoff must also say

- Which **AUDIT DEBT** items this pass **corrected** (quote log lines used)
- Which **AUDIT DEBT** items stay **OPEN** (honest — no "full re-audit" lip service)

## Builder uses AUDIT DEBT

- If handoff omits AUDIT DEBT section → treat like thin handoff; cross-check logs harder.
- Do **not** implement audit guesses that repeat an OPEN audit-debt pattern (e.g. "probably ImGui" without Grok cite).

## Builder does not edit AUDIT_DEBT.md unless coordinator asks — **Auditor** maintains it on FAIL.
